{"base_rate":0.3841642228739003,"brier":0.15524545454545455,"bss":0.3437987386404944,"bss_hi":0.4487545703726794,"bss_lo":0.23495958930956523,"country":"NO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.12621700879765393,"ess":332.0724081919796,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Oslo</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Oslo rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 682 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nOSLO - BLINDERN PLU, 3.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.34, ranked 7 of\n15 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(5&ndash;11) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>177</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>94</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>208</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Oslo\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.1,379.94350282485874 76.90510638297872,343.27659574468083 147.95764705882354,253.52941176470588 261.1415384615384,130.0 360.0125714285714,44.0 410.04278846153846,18.0 410.04278846153846,25.0 360.0125714285714,101.19999999999999 261.1415384615384,214.0 147.95764705882354,323.11764705882354 76.90510638297872,378.1276595744681 58.1,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"242.1642228739003\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"242.1642228739003\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.1,365.54802259887003 76.90510638297872,351.02127659574467 147.95764705882354,317.7647058823529 261.1415384615384,236.4 360.0125714285714,168.79999999999998 410.04278846153846,89.75\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 177 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.1\" cy=\"365.54802259887003\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 5%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 94 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"76.90510638297872\" cy=\"351.02127659574467\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 25%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"147.95764705882354\" cy=\"317.7647058823529\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 57%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 65 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"261.1415384615384\" cy=\"236.4\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 59% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"360.0125714285714\" cy=\"168.79999999999998\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 208 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.04278846153846\" cy=\"89.75\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(38%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Oslo the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>summer</b> (0.38) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (0.25).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>212</td><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'>0.245</td><td class='num'>13.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.318</td><td class='num'>10.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>152</td><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'>0.329</td><td class='num'>14.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>143</td><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'>0.376</td><td class='num'>10.8%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":59.9139,"lon":10.7522,"n":682,"n_cities":15,"name":"Oslo","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0002824858757062147,"n":177,"obs":0.04519774011299435,"sig":true},{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.05340425531914892,"n":94,"obs":0.0851063829787234,"sig":false},{"hi":0.43,"lo":0.14,"mean":0.25411764705882356,"n":68,"obs":0.17647058823529413,"sig":false},{"hi":0.75,"lo":0.43,"mean":0.5738461538461538,"n":65,"obs":0.4,"sig":true},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.75,"mean":0.8531428571428571,"n":70,"obs":0.5857142857142857,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9944711538461538,"n":208,"obs":0.8028846153846154,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.6,"rank":7,"rank_hi":11.0,"rank_lo":5.0,"reliability":0.022678846093103958,"resolution":0.10411300606174763,"slug":"oslo","station":"OSLO - BLINDERN PLU","timezone":"Europe/Oslo"}